**Step 1 – Rewrite the right‑hand side**

\[
\begin{aligned}
y'&=- \frac{2\sin(2x)\,\arctan x}{\cos^{2}2x}
      -\frac{2\operatorname{acot}x\;\displaystyle\left.\frac{d}{d\xi}\cot\xi\right|_{\xi=2x}}{\cot^{2}2x}
      -\frac{1}{(x^{2}+1)\cos2x}
      -\frac{1}{(x^{2}+1)\cot2x}.
\end{aligned}
\]

Since \(\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\xi}\cot\xi=-\csc^{2}\xi\) and \(\cot^{2}2x=\frac{\cos^{2}2x}{\sin^{2}2x}\),

\[
-\frac{2\operatorname{acot}x\;(-\csc^{2}2x)}{\cot^{2}2x}
   =\frac{2\operatorname{acot}x\;\csc^{2}2x}{\cot^{2}2x}
   =2\operatorname{acot}x\;\frac{1/\sin^{2}2x}{\cos^{2}2x/\sin^{2}2x}
   =2\operatorname{acot}x\;\sec^{2}2x .
\]

Also \(\displaystyle\frac{1}{\cot2x}= \tan2x\).  
Hence

\[
y'=-\frac{2\sin(2x)\,\arctan x}{\cos^{2}2x}
    +2\operatorname{acot}x\;\sec^{2}2x
    -\frac{1}{(x^{2}+1)\cos2x}
    -\frac{\tan2x}{x^{2}+1}.
\]

